he False branch of line 147. Good for branch coverage.\n\nTest 8: explicit_json with no lexer found and valid JSON body:\n```python\ndef test_get_lexer_explicit_json_no_lexer():\n    lexer = get_lexer('x-foo/bar', explicit_json=True, body='{\"a\": 1}')\n    assert isinstance(lexer, pygments.lexers.JsonLexer)\n```\nHere lexer is None after loops \u2192 condition True (not lexer) \u2192 json.loads OK \u2192 line 154. This covers `not lexer` part of the condition. Also covers 129-130? 'bar' doesn't contain json. Let me use a mime with json in subtype but unresolvable: 'x-foo/json' \u2014 subtype 'json' contains 'json' \u2192 line 130 covered. mime_types = ['x-foo/json'] \u2192 ClassNotFound. names = ['json'] \u2192 get_lexer_by_name('json') \u2192 JsonLexer! So lexer would be JsonLexer already at line 143. Then condition: lexer is JsonLexer, not TextLexer, not None \u2192 False. Hmm, that doesn't cover the `not lexer` path.\n\nTo cover `not lexer` in condition: need all lookups to fail, then explicit_json with valid body. E.g., mime = 'x-foo/bar-baz-qux', explicit_json=True, body='{\"a\": 1}' \u2192 lexer None \u2192 condition True \u2192 json.loads OK \u2192 JsonLexer. That covers `not lexer` branch.\n\nAnd to cover line 130 ('json' in subtype \u2192 append 'json'): mime = 'x-foo/json' \u2192 names = ['json'] \u2192 resolves to JsonLexer via name. That covers 129-130 and 143. \n\nAlso need to cover the case where 'json' in subtype and the name loop's get_lexer_by_name('json') is reached \u2014 that's covered by 'x-foo/json'.\n\nNow, what about line 121's lexer_names.extend and line 122-124's mime_types.extend \u2014 covered by test 2 ('application/vnd.api+json').\n\nWhat about the branch where '+' in subtype AND mimetype lookup fails for all AND name lookup: e.g., 'application/vnd.foo+barbaz' \u2192 mime_types: ['application/vnd.foo+barbaz', 'application/vnd.foo', 'application/barbaz'] all fail; names: ['vnd.foo', 'barbaz'] both fail \u2192 None. That covers 145 again